/* The UI string catalogue -- one line per translatable string.
 *
 * Included twice: once by ui_i18n.h to build the `ui_str_t` enum, and once
 * per language by ui_i18n.c to build that language's table. Adding a string
 * means adding exactly one line here; nothing else has to be kept in step.
 *
 *     UI_STR(NAME, "English", u8"Japanese")
 *
 * The Japanese column is also what generates the font subset: every character
 * that appears here is baked into components/ui/src/fonts/ui_font_ja_*.c by
 * tools/gen_ja_fonts.py. Run that script after touching Japanese text, or the
 * new characters will render as boxes.
 *
 * Both columns must carry the same printf conversions in the same order -- a
 * mismatched "%s" here is a crash, not a typo. tools/check_strings.py checks
 * that for every line.
 */

